<Base title="Privacy and ownership" description="Where App Composer data lives, how demo moderation and deletion work, and why credentials and assistant keys stay out of specifications."><h1>Privacy and data ownership</h1><p>Reviewed 14 October 2026.</p><section class="section"><h2>Public browsing</h2><p>No account is required. Init drafts and decision paths are saved in this browser’s local storage. Use “Start a fresh draft” or clear browser site data to remove them. Exported specs contain your entered configuration; inspect them before sharing. They must not contain passwords, tokens or private personal records.</p><h2>Tutorial progress</h2><p>The follow-along tutorial saves the current lesson and self-reported observations in this browser. It stores no free-text notes or account credentials and does not upload those observations. Use “Clear my learning notes” in the tutorial to remove them. Setup reports remain separate and are remembered only through the report viewer’s own choice.</p><h2>Photo Guestbook and Linkarooie</h2><p>Uploads and moderation require the invited owner credential. Pending originals remain in private R2 storage. Only currently approved contributions are served publicly. Hiding revokes controlled requests; deletion removes the original and leaves a moderation tombstone. Responses use no-store. Files people already downloaded and third-party copies cannot be recalled.</p><p>Original demo artwork is labelled. The hosted demo is not a public submission service; do not upload personal or sensitive images to test it.</p><h2>App activity</h2><p>The public leaderboard stores daily totals of successful app home-page requests, original photo opens and completed Link Check inspections. It does not store individual events, visitor identifiers, entered URLs, searches or vault data. Totals expire after 35 days, with a daily recording limit of 1,000 per app/action/version. Shared per-location recording limits drop excess events. Reloads and bots can count; optional publishers can miss requests. Forks are disconnected by default. Verification probes are excluded.</p><h2>Credentials and logs</h2><p>Cloudflare and GitHub credentials stay in the authorised agent/runtime. Owner credentials and encryption settings are runtime secrets. Portable specs do not carry them. Cloudflare processes request metadata and retains bounded operational logs according to the operator’s account settings. The existing Cloudflare zone injects Cloudflare Web Analytics on public pages. It is separate from saved drafts and does not receive owner credentials or vault plaintext. The encrypted state mini-app blocks that script with its content security policy.</p><h2>Portable AI State</h2><p>The fictional demo encrypts locally with a key derived from an owner-held passphrase. Plaintext and the key are never uploaded by this tool. Clipboard disclosure to a model is an explicit separate action. It remains a synthetic-only demonstration pending the complete security and interoperability gates.</p></section></Base>
